{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":27199,"duration_api_ms":28115,"num_turns":11,"result":"I wrote the script at `src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`, but I haven't run or validated it. The dry run needed approval that wasn't granted. You can check it with `sudo bpftrace -d src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`.\n\nIt attaches to the `power:cpu_frequency` tracepoint and works like this:\n- **While running:** it prints a line for each frequency change with the time, CPU, old frequency and new frequency in MHz.\n- **On Ctrl-C:** bpftrace dumps the total milliseconds each CPU spent at each frequency, the number of changes per CPU, and a histogram of the new frequencies.\n\nThe tracepoint only fires when the driver actually changes frequency. It may stay quiet on VMs or under `intel_pstate` in active mode.\n\nI put it in `49-cpufreq` because `48-energy` is the last numbered tutorial. I didn't add a README or Makefile. Tell me if you want them or a different location.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c3a58e6e-8fb1-40c9-a091-62dc9ef6316c","total_cost_usd":0.1202638,"usage":{"input_tokens":20,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3328,"cache_read_input_tokens":237576,"output_tokens":2400,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3328},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":330,"cache_read_input_tokens":28328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":281,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":281,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":351,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000451,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":20,"outputTokens":2400,"cacheReadInputTokens":237576,"cacheCreationInputToke